          "merged_at": null
        },
        "body": "## Summary\n\nWhen an OpenAI-compatible stream ends with `finish_reason: \"length\"`, partial tool-call arguments can be repaired into a valid-looking `tool_call`. This can cause downstream tools to execute with silently truncated input.\n\nThis change preserves the raw arguments as an `invalid_tool_call` whenever the assembled stream ended because of the token limit. Normal completed tool calls retain their existing behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added a deterministic `ChatModelStream` regression test covering truncated arguments, tool-call identity, raw arguments, and the `length` finish reason.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- The focused Vitest, oxfmt, and oxlint commands could not complete because this checkout has no installed `node_modules`.\n\nRelated issue: #11469\n",
